WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.859
Next question today is, hey, David, it's pretty
clear at this point that horrible presidents

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:11.490
don't really increase voter turnout that much
from people who are desperate to get them

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.490
out of office.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.540
What actually does or would increase voter
turnout?

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.680
Yeah, so here's the thing.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.810
I actually, I believe that the activism that
has been inspired by Donald Trump is real

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:27.450
and, uh, uh, is or at least was substantive.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:35.190
The problem is that people, um, adjust very
quickly to the new status quo.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.140
And it's been a couple of years now that Donald
Trump has been around and things that would

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.170
have been scandals in his first month, no
longer even register as scandals.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.079
There has been a creeping normalization.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.310
So I actually do believe that an acutely cartoonishly
horrible president does inspire people to

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:52.310
vote.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:56.110
The problem is the election isn't held three
months after the inauguration, it's four years

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:00.239
later and that's a long time for things to
become re normalized and I think that that's

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.239
the problem.

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.030
But your point is well taken, which is I don't
believe that a lot of the activism and enthusiasm

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:10.010
and energy that we saw in the marches and
the protests after Donald Trump's election

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.270
and inauguration, I think a lot of it is faded
and a lot of those people are not going to

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:17.370
vote in November of 2020 so what does increase
voter turnout?

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:21.340
We have a context here in the United States
of non mandatory voting.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.590
Along with that.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.409
We see very low voter turnout, often not even
50% I think sometimes in midterms we have

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:32.990
40 to 45 maybe in some presidential elections
it gets to 55 I'm going from memory.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.850
I don't exactly remember, but it is a very
low turnout compared to many other western

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.979
countries.

00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:42.080
Usually the discussion about increasing voter
turnout is at the micro level.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.150
I'll give you some examples.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.500
Automatic voter registration.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.540
Okay.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.040
Automatic voter registration does seem to
have an effect on increasing voter turnout.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.100
That's a good thing.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.710
We should enable same day registration, meaning
even if you didn't have the forethought to

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:01.810
register to vote six months before the election,
if you decide on election day, hey, you know

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:02.920
what, it's election day.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.150
I'm going to vote.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.130
You should be able to register on that day.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.709
That does increase voter turnout.

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:16.560
Voting by mail, absentee voting without requiring
a reason helps voter turnout, allowing people

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.090
not to have to justify, you know, I have limited
mobility or I'm going to be out of the country.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:27.420
I want to vote by mail with an absentee ballot
ballot allowing absentee ballot with no required

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.870
justification increases voter turnout.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.459
Now one that historically does not seem to
increase voter turnout is early voting.

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:41.129
Um, we talk a lot about restrictions on early
voting, strategically meant to help Republicans

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:45.189
as part of the voter suppression package that
we've seen from the Republican Party.

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:52.040
And we need to fight that any effort to disproportionately
disenfranchise democratic poor, non white

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.401
voters, we need to fight against it.

00:02:53.401 --> 00:02:58.419
But a couple of studies that we have now suggest
that early voting does not seem to, in total

00:02:58.419 --> 00:03:01.059
increased voter turnout making election day.

00:03:01.059 --> 00:03:03.340
A national holiday is an idea that's thrown
out there.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.379
I'm up for any of these that are demonstrated
to increase voter turnout, but I think we're

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:08.699
thinking too small.

00:03:08.699 --> 00:03:09.699
Okay.

00:03:09.699 --> 00:03:17.370
We need to be increasing voter turnout by
educating people who are more connected to

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.379
the importance of participating in elections.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:21.379
That's it.

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:22.379
Okay.

00:03:22.379 --> 00:03:29.209
So it's not, I mean, okay, listen, the absentee
voting with not without a required a justification.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.230
Let's do it.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.230
Okay?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.409
But we need to be starting with 12 year olds
in middle school.

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:38.339
And I talk about we need to be teaching critical
thinking at an early age.

00:03:38.339 --> 00:03:41.720
We need to be thinking, uh, teaching civics
at an early age.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.920
We need to be teaching up basics of philosophy
and thinking about how to think at an early

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.920
age.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.370
This will generate people who are more involved
and better thinkers and it is going to help

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.359
the left by the way, because the more people
that are thinking in the more educated people

00:03:55.359 --> 00:03:59.180
are in these areas, the more likely they are
to vote for left wing candidates.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:04.359
But it's much more difficult to convince a
22 year old who's never voted.

00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:06.199
It matters.

00:04:06.199 --> 00:04:07.480
You should vote.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:15.059
Go and register then just raising kids starting
in middle school, who integrate the importance

00:04:15.059 --> 00:04:18.370
of our participating in our political system.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.200
This includes voting, but this includes being
activists.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.540
This includes writing letters when necessary.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:28.520
This includes protesting and, uh, massing
and urban centers when necessary.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:33.190
So I think that the best way to increase voter
turnout, we can play around the edges with

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.810
automatic registration, same day registration.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.810
And all of this stuff.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:45.020
The real way to increase voter turnout is
to from an early age in grain, in every student,

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.770
the importance of voting and make it the default.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.520
Not some people choose to vote in, some don't.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.520
You should vote.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.640
The default should be you register and you
vote.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:59.640
Barring some really good reason not to go
out and vote, that's going to increase voter

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.050
turnout much, much more than any of these
little changes we might make around the edges.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.050
Let me know what you think.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.870
Um, big picture.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.820
Let me know what you think at the micro level
in terms of the specific changes that can

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.960
be made, what will increase voter turnout
and what will not.

